 **Data Structures:**
-*   **NeRF Model ($F_\Theta$):** A multi-layer perceptron (MLP) mapping 3D coordinates and viewing directions to color and density. The implementation uses a hidden layer dimension of 128 [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Camera Parameters ($\pi_i$):** For each image $i$, parameters are defined as $\pi_i = (\hat{f}, \hat{\phi}_i, \hat{t}_i)$, where $\hat{f}$ is the shared focal length, $\hat{\phi}_i \in \mathbb{R}^3$ is the axis-angle rotation vector, and $\hat{t}_i \in \mathbb{R}^3$ is the translation vector [S1, unofficial].
+*   **NeRF Model $F_\Theta$:** A multi-layer perceptron (MLP). The hidden layer dimension is reduced to 128 for computational efficiency [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Camera Parameters $\pi_i$:**
+    *   $\hat{f}$: Scalar focal length.
+    *   $\hat{\phi}_i \in \mathbb{R}^3$: Axis-angle representation of rotation. The direction is the rotation axis, and the magnitude is the angle.
+    *   $\hat{t}_i \in \mathbb{R}^3$: Translation vector (camera position).
+    *   Rotation matrix $R_i$ is derived from $\hat{\phi}_i$ using Rodrigues' formula [S1, unofficial].
 
